      "answer": {
        "question": "Are we on pace to hit goal, and where do we land by election day if nothing changes?",
        "answer": "We are ahead of goal to date (103.3% [table:v_office_pace] of the goal-to-date), but if nothing changes we land short of the full goal by about 3,300 doors [table:v_office_pace], at roughly 94.6% [table:v_office_pace] of goal by election day.\n\n- Program doors to date: 33,503 [table:v_office_pace] vs goal-to-date 32,431 [table:v_office_pace] = 103.3% [table:v_office_pace]\n- Projected total by election day: 57,329 [table:v_office_pace] vs goal 60,632 [table:v_office_pace] = 94.6% [table:v_office_pace], a shortfall of 3,303 doors [table:v_office_pace]\n- Northside is the only office projected to beat goal: 23,583 [table:v_office_pace] vs 22,675 [table:v_office_pace] = 104% [table:v_office_pace] (+908 [table:v_office_pace])\n- Harbor: 19,150 [table:v_office_pace] vs 20,157 [table:v_office_pace] = 95% [table:v_office_pace] (\u22121,007 [table:v_office_pace])\n- Eastgate is the biggest gap: 14,596 [table:v_office_pace] vs 17,800 [table:v_office_pace] = 82% [table:v_office_pace] (\u22123,204 [table:v_office_pace])\n- To close the gap we'd need about 4.1 [table:v_office_pace] extra shifts per day program-wide (Eastgate 4.4 [table:v_office_pace], Harbor 1.3 [table:v_office_pace], Northside 0 [table:v_office_pace])\n\nHow it's worked out: projection = doors to date + last 7 days' average daily doors (1,489.1 [table:v_office_pace]) \u00d7 16 [table:v_office_pace] knocking days left (Oct 19 to Nov 3); a negative projected_vs_goal is the shortfall [table:v_office_pace].",
