      "answer": {
        "question": "Are we on pace for the registration goal, and what cards per hour do we need from here?",
        "answer": "We're slightly under pace: the program is projected to collect 5,311 valid cards against a goal of 5,370, a shortfall of 59 cards, and we need to work at 2.96 valid cards per hour from here.\n\n- Program goal: 5,370 cards; valid cards to date: 3,669 (3,781 collected, 112 duplicates) [table:v_vr_pace]\n- Projected valid cards by the Oct 30 deadline: 5,311, which is 59 short of goal [table:v_vr_pace]\n- Cards per hour needed from here (program-wide): 2.96, vs 2.86 in the last 7 days [table:v_vr_pace]\n- 12 days left to the Oct 30 deadline; average daily registration hours last 7 days: 47.9 [table:v_vr_pace]\n- By office, Northside is also under pace (projected 2,137 vs goal 2,170; needs 3.52/hr vs 3.35 last 7 days), while Eastgate (1,325 vs 1,380) and Harbor (1,849 vs 1,820) are close or slightly over [table:v_vr_pace]\n\nHow it's worked out: cards per hour needed = cards still needed (goal minus valid cards) divided by expected hours before the deadline (last 7 days' average daily hours \u00d7 days left); an office is under the needed rate when its last-7-days rate is below the program-wide rate needed [doc:registration-drive#cards-per-hour].",
