          "name": "under 30 seconds apart",
          "expected": [
            "30 seconds",
            "thirty seconds"
          ],
          "matched": true
        }
      ],
      "answer": {
        "question": "What counts as flash knocking under our QC rules?",
        "answer": "Flash knocking is recording doors faster than a person can physically walk to them and knock \u2014 specifically, 10 or more consecutive knocks recorded less than 30 seconds apart.\n\n- Threshold: 10+ consecutive knocks each less than 30 seconds apart [doc:qc-rules#flash-knocking]\n- Confirmed flash knocking is rolled back: the knocks in the window no longer count as doors or contacts [doc:qc-rules#flash-knocking]\n- A whole shift recorded this way is rolled back in full [doc:qc-rules#flash-knocking]\n- Rollbacks happen after the day's client report is pulled, so they never change a report already sent [doc:counting-doors#rollbacks]\n- Every open flag needs a conversation with the canvasser before their next shift; 2+ flash knocking flags in a week for the same canvasser go to the field director [doc:qc-rules#what-happens-after-a-flag]",
        "refused": false,
        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "name": "search_documents",
            "args": {
              "query": "flash knocking QC rule definition"
            },
            "ok": true,
            "result": "4 passages: qc-rules#flash-knocking, counting-doors#rollbacks, qc-rules#what-happens-after-a-flag, qc-rules#qc-rate"
          }
        ],
        "sources": [
          {
            "type": "passage",
            "doc": "qc-rules#flash-knocking",
            "text": "Flash knocking is recording doors faster than a person can walk to them and knock. A shift is flagged when 10 or more consecutive knocks are recorded less than 30 seconds apart. Confirmed flash knocking is rolled back: the knocks in the window no longer count as doors or contacts. A whole shift recorded this way is rolled back in full."
          },
          {
            "type": "passage",
            "doc": "counting-doors#rollbacks",
            "text": "When QC confirms flash knocking, the knocks in the flagged window are rolled back: they stay in the data with rolled_back = true but are removed from doors and contacts. Rollbacks happen after the day's client report has been pulled, so they never change a report that was already sent."
          },
          {
            "type": "passage",
            "doc": "qc-rules#what-happens-after-a-flag",
